  "text": "### Interest Rate Mechanics  \n**The Formula:**\nBoE Base Rate + 2.5% (FirstUK margin) = Your Rate  \n**Example:**\n- BoE is 4.0%\n- FirstUK adds 2.5%\n- Your rate = 6.5% AER  \n**If BoE Changes:**\n- BoE rises to 4.5% → Your rate rises to 7.0%\n- BoE falls to 3.5% → Your rate falls to 6.0%  \n**Why This Is Good:**\nYour 2.5% margin never changes. You're always getting a competitive rate without FirstUK cutting margin.",
